  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...A slow moving cold front will cross the area through \ntoday bringing several rounds of rain, heavy at times.  \n\nAs of 7 AM this morning, a diffuse cold front was located over NW NJ \nextending south and westward through SE PA into Delmarva. There has \nbeen an initial round of heavy rainfall with embedded thunderstorms \nthat's been moving through and this has brought rainfall amounts of \n1.5 to 2.5 inches over portions of NJ running from northern \nGloucester County north and eastward through portions of Camden, \nBurlington, Ocean, and Monmouth Counties. This has even resulted in \nsome instances of flash flooding early this morning. Motorists are \nurged to use extra caution and allow extra time for their morning \ncommute. Following this initial round of heavy rainfall, there will \nlikely be a bit of a lull with just some lighter rain until another \nround of potentially heavier showers moves through around late \nmorning into this afternoon. With the cold front continuing to \nslowly push southeastward with time, expect that heaviest rain with \nthis second batch to again be focused mainly near and especially \nsoutheast of the urban corridor towards the coast. It also should \nnot be as heavy as what we've been seeing early this morning as the \ngreater moisture and instability will be getting pushed south and \neastward with the front so any additional flooding should be fairly \nlocalized. \n\nConditions will gradually improve as we go through this afternoon \nand especially for areas N/W of the I-95 corridor. Remaining areas \nmay not see substantial improvement until the evening hours.\n\nThe cold front departs offshore tonight, with dry conditions \nreturning for much of the area. However, guidance indicates an upper-\nlow will track eastward across northern portions of the area on \nSaturday. This will lead to a lingering chance for some light rain \nnorth of I-78, with the highest chances (40-50%) across the Poconos \nand far northern NJ. By Sunday morning, the upper-low will be east \nof the area bringing a return of dry conditions to the region along \nwith cooler temperatures.",
